; --- Four more stalls, facing the east-west cross-lane ------------------------------------------------
; ⚠️ These are named StallX*, NOT StallW*/StallE*, and they carry NO Counter child. That is the whole
; signal: the six stalls with a Counter at local (2.2, 0, 0) are 38L's mounts and their transforms are
; frozen; these four are set dressing and may be moved by anyone. Naming them StallW4.. would have made
; the contract ambiguous the first time someone read the file quickly.
;
; They exist because the cross-lane was a paved lane with nothing on it. Six stalls in two rows 18 m
; apart read as an avenue; ten stalls around a crossroads read as a market — which is the difference
; the first pass of this rebuild still had not closed.

