; --- The three silent villagers 38K placed here are GONE (38L) ------------------------------------
; They were authored for one stated reason - "no people in 2,704 m2" - and twelve merchants answer it
; better than three bystanders did. Two of the three also had to go on their own merits: the Porter wore
; npc_townsman, which is Quaternius's Worker, which is a hi-vis vest and a hard hat, and it does not
; survive being looked at from three metres in a medieval market.
;
; What 38K's note promised 38L is still true and now moot: the villagers kept their interactable slot
; free so a merchant could be dropped onto one. In the event the merchants got their own mounts at the
; stalls, which is where a merchant belongs.
;
; ⚠️ npc_townsman.glb is now referenced by nothing. It is left in assets/models/ rather than deleted -
; it is a valid CC0 body and some future modern-dress or labourer role may want it - but do not reach
; for it to dress anyone in the Ember Crown.

; --- The market's own sound. Two positional emitters on the spine, so the murmur swells as the player
; --- walks in and fades as they leave — which an amb.* bed can never do, because those are 2D and
; --- chosen globally from weather / in-town / clock, and SafeZones cannot tell this district from the
; --- square one street north. See AmbientEmitterComponent's own note.

