script = ExtResource("7_ambient")
CueId = "sfx.ambient.market"
IntervalSeconds = 9.0
IntervalJitter = 0.55
Radius = 24.0

; ====================================================================================================
; THE ROSTER (Phase 38L) - ten resident merchants and two travellers.
;
; ⚠️ ALL TWELVE ARE OUTSIDE Nav, like every other actor in this cell. A body inside the
; NavigationRegion3D carves a hole in the navmesh where a person is standing.
;
; ⚠️ THE TEN RESIDENTS TALK; THE TWO TRAVELLERS CARRY A VendorComponent. That split is forced, not
; stylistic. DialogueSession evaluates the ShopOpen/ShopClosed conditions through ShopHours.IsOpenAt
; alone - HOURS, NOT PRESENCE - and the only thing that hides an away merchant and zeroes her collider
; is VendorComponent.ApplyPresence. A traveller wired through a dialogue choice would stand at her cart
; every day of a five-day cycle with a working trade line, which is 38J's mechanic inverted. Hesk in
; town_hub.tscn took the same route for the same reason.
;   The cost, and it is real: a VendorComponent's ShopId lives in this .tscn and --validate CANNOT read
;   it. A typo gives NO PROMPT AT ALL rather than an error. If Sera or Quill is ever silently unusable,
;   check those two strings before anything else. The ten residents' shop ids live in their dialogue
;   .tres files, where the validator does read them - which is most of why they talk.
;
; ⚠️ ONE INTERACTABLE PER ENTITY. EntityNode.GetComponent<T> returns the first child match, so a
; merchant carries EITHER a DialogueComponent OR a VendorComponent and never both.
;
; ⚠️ BodyMeshPath = "Model" on every one. The default is "BodyMesh" and a scene NPC that keeps it
; T-poses in place with nothing logged.
;
; A merchant stands BETWEEN her stall and its Counter, facing the aisle - so the Counter at the stall's
; local (2.2, 0, 0) is the customer's side of the boards, which is what 38K's contract meant by it.
; These are starting poses only: each resident's ScheduleComponent walks them to their stall at opening
; and a couple of metres behind it at closing, and every one of those destinations is CELL-LOCAL
; against schedule Origin (0, 0, 46).
;
; ⚠️ EIGHT BODIES FOR TWELVE MERCHANTS. assets/library/ holds exactly two unused CC0 models a medieval
; market can wear (men/adventurer, women/animated_woman_2, shipped here as npc_merchant_m/f); the other
; five unused women are CC-BY 3.0 and this project is CC0-only, and the remaining men are a business
; suit, a hoodie and jeans-and-sneakers. Four bodies therefore appear twice, paired as far apart as the
; square allows. Closing the gap needs an open-web pull of Quaternius's RPG Character Pack, which 38L
; did not make.
; ====================================================================================================

